• Copy Nested Levels That Need Updating

• Use map() for Immutable Item Updates

• Use filter() for Immutable Removal

• Use Spread Syntax for Copies

• Use Functional State Updates When the New Value Depends on Previous State

• Console Mutation Does NOT Mean React Processed a State Update


================================================================================
QUICK REVISION - MUTATION VS IMMUTABILITY
================================================================================

MUTATION - WRONG:

Existing State Object
        ↓
Modify Same Object
        ↓
Same Reference
        ↓
State Setter May Be Bypassed
        ↓
Unreliable UI Behavior


IMMUTABLE UPDATE - CORRECT:

Existing State
        ↓
Create New Value/Object/Array
        ↓
Call State Setter
        ↓
React Processes Update
        ↓
Component Re-renders as Needed
        ↓
UI Reflects State


================================================================================
QUICK REVISION - OBJECT UPDATE
================================================================================

WRONG:

user.name = 'John Smith'


RIGHT:

setUser({
  ...user,
  name: 'John Smith'
})


FLOW:

Existing User
     ↓
Spread Existing Properties
     ↓
Replace name
     ↓
Create New Object
     ↓
setUser()
     ↓
React Processes Update


================================================================================
QUICK REVISION - ARRAY OPERATIONS
================================================================================

+----------------+--------------------+--------------------------------------+
| OPERATION      | AVOID ON STATE     | PREFER                               |
+----------------+--------------------+--------------------------------------+
| Add            | push()             | [...items, newItem]                  |
| Remove Last    | pop()              | slice(0, -1)                         |
| Remove Item    | splice()           | filter()                             |
| Add First      | unshift()          | [newItem, ...items]                  |
| Remove First   | shift()            | slice(1)                             |
| Update Item    | item.prop = value  | map() + {...item}                    |
| Sort           | sort() directly    | [...items].sort()                    |
| Reverse        | reverse() directly | [...items].reverse()                 |
+----------------+--------------------+--------------------------------------+


================================================================================
QUICK REVISION - NESTED OBJECT
================================================================================

STATE:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

const [user, setUser] = useState({

  name: 'John',

  address: {
    city: 'New York',
    country: 'USA'
  }

})


WRONG:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

user.address.city = 'Boston'


RIGHT:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

setUser({
  ...user,

  address: {
    ...user.address,
    city: 'Boston'
  }
})


WHY?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

New outer object
      +
New modified nested object
      ↓
No mutation of previous state


================================================================================
QUICK REFERENCE TABLE
================================================================================

+--------------------------+---------------------------------------------+
| CONCEPT                  | REMEMBER                                    |
+--------------------------+---------------------------------------------+
| State                    | Treat it as read-only                       |
| State Setter             | Requests a React state update               |
| Mutation                 | Changes existing object/array               |
| Immutability             | Creates replacement values                  |
| Object Update            | Use spread syntax                          |
| Array Add                | [...array, item]                            |
| Array Remove             | filter()                                   |
| Array Update             | map()                                      |
| Nested Update            | Copy every modified nesting level           |
| push/pop/splice          | Mutate an array                            |
| sort/reverse             | Mutate an array when called directly        |
| Reference                | Identity of object/array                    |
| Functional Setter        | Useful when next state depends on previous |
| Console Log              | Doesn't prove React processed state update |
| key                      | Identifies list elements, separate concern |
+--------------------------+---------------------------------------------+


================================================================================
ONE-LINE MEMORY FORMULAS
================================================================================

WRONG:

State → Mutate Existing Value → Problems


RIGHT:

State → Create Updated Value → Setter → React → UI


OBJECT:

{...oldObject, changedProperty: newValue}


ARRAY ADD:

[...oldArray, newItem]


ARRAY REMOVE:

oldArray.filter(...)


ARRAY UPDATE:

oldArray.map(...)


NESTED OBJECT:

{
  ...state,
  nested: {
    ...state.nested,
    property: newValue
  }
}


PREVIOUS STATE UPDATE:

setCount(previous =>
  previous + 1
)


MOST IMPORTANT RULE:

DO NOT MUTATE STATE DIRECTLY.
CREATE THE NEXT STATE VALUE AND USE THE STATE SETTER.


